sequenceDiagram
    actor User as CLI User
    participant BIC as BuildImageCommand
    participant RIR as RunnerImageRenderer
    participant IB as AWS Image Builder
    participant CF as AWS CloudFormation
    participant EC2 as AWS EC2
    participant SSM as AWS SSM

    User->>BIC: baas admin image build [--extension ext.yaml]
    Note over BIC: ConfigService.load()<br/>deployer credentials (aws.profile), NOT aws.operatorProfile --<br/>this needs imagebuilder:*, ssm:PutParameter and a widened iam:PassRole
    opt --extension
        Note over BIC: read the file, strip its #35; baas-extension-base marker,<br/>comments only = no extension, over 4096 bytes -> exit 1<br/>before any AWS call
    end
    BIC->>RIR: render /templates/runner-image.yaml
    RIR-->>BIC: base version, parent AMI name, base AWSTOE document

    BIC->>CF: describeStacks -> deployed image parameters
    CF-->>BIC: extension, derived versions, base, parent, contract
    Note over BIC: bundled base version lower than the deployed RunnerImageVersion -><br/>exit 1 naming both and the CLI upgrade, nothing submitted (U39).<br/>Replacing the component deletes the newer version, so nothing else would refuse it.
    opt --extension
        Note over BIC: deployed extension H and the file's marker is not H -><br/>exit 1, nothing submitted. The stack holds the only copy,<br/>so a stale push would discard someone else's extension.<br/>No extension deployed -> any file is accepted.
    end
    BIC->>EC2: describeImages(owner=amazon, name=<parent AMI name>, x86_64)
    EC2-->>BIC: exactly one image in this region, else exit 1 naming release and region
    Note over BIC: RunnerImageParameters.plan: label = base or base+ext.sha256[0:8],<br/>contract rendered with the label and the runner's Java floor,<br/>extension and recipe versions = deployed + 1 when their content changed

    BIC->>IB: listComponents(owner=Self, filter name=<prefix>-component-runner)
    Note over BIC,IB: deliberately WITHOUT byName: that collapses every version into<br/>one row with no version field and an ARN ending in a literal x.x.x,<br/>so the version filter matches nothing and the preflight passes blind
    IB-->>BIC: component versions
    opt declared imageVersion already registered
        BIC->>IB: listComponentBuildVersions + getComponent
        IB-->>BIC: registered component document
        Note over BIC: content differs -> exit 1 naming imageVersion in<br/>infra/runner-image.yaml. No build is started: a component<br/>is immutable at a version, so the stack update would be<br/>rejected ~1 minute in, naming the resource and not the fix.
    end

    BIC->>CF: updateStack(core template, 8 image parameters)
    Note over BIC,CF: only the image parameters are sent, and every other parameter is<br/>carried forward with UsePreviousValue, or a stack deployed with<br/>--use-existing-vpc would silently flip back to building a VPC.<br/>Without --extension the deployed extension is re-sent unchanged.
    CF-->>BIC: UPDATE_COMPLETE (or "no updates are to be performed")
    BIC->>CF: describeStacks -> RunnerImagePipelineArn
    CF-->>BIC: pipeline ARN (via !GetAtt .Arn, never !Ref)

    BIC->>SSM: getParameter(/<prefix>/runner/ami-id)
    SSM-->>BIC: previous AMI id, or empty on a first build

    BIC->>IB: startImagePipelineExecution(pipelineArn)
    IB-->>BIC: imageBuildVersionArn
    Note over IB,EC2: Image Builder launches a c5.large build host under ImageBuildRole and<br/>runs the base (pinned Corretto, perf for uname -r, async-profiler,<br/>sysctl + grubby tunables), the extension if any, then the contract's<br/>build phase (writes the label). It snapshots the AMI, then boots a<br/>test instance from it and runs the contract's test phase: Java floor,<br/>aws, async-profiler, perf = kernel, label, the two sysctls.<br/>Any failed check fails the build.
    loop poll every 30s
        BIC->>IB: getImage(imageBuildVersionArn)
        IB-->>BIC: CREATING | BUILDING | DISTRIBUTING | AVAILABLE | FAILED
    end
    Note over BIC: FAILED -> throw with Image Builder's own reason.<br/>Pointer and previous AMI are untouched.

    BIC->>EC2: describeImages(newAmiId)
    EC2-->>BIC: tags set by the DistributionConfiguration
    opt identity tags absent
        BIC->>EC2: createTags(baas-image-version = label, baas-parent-ami)
    end

    BIC->>SSM: putParameter(/<prefix>/runner/ami-id = newAmiId, String)
    Note over BIC,SSM: REPOINT BEFORE RETIRE. Deregistering first would aim the<br/>pointer at a deleted AMI for the whole ~15-minute build,<br/>failing every job launched in that window.
    opt a previous, different AMI existed
        BIC->>EC2: describeImages(previousAmiId) -> snapshot ids
        BIC->>EC2: deregisterImage(previousAmiId)
        BIC->>EC2: deleteSnapshot(each) -- else the snapshots bill forever
    end
    BIC-->>User: label, new AMI id, parent AMI, extension hash, pointer path -- exit 0
